@@s009 Testing the LazyList
@@s010 Week 6, exercises 1–10. The role is reversed: the LazyList is already there, the test file is yours to write. The grader runs your tests on many broken LazyLists (the <b>mutants</b>): every mutant you make fail is worth points. The right LazyList, <code>lazyList00</code>, must pass all your tests, otherwise you lose 35%. Only <code>Exercises.scala</code> is handed in. Theory: <a href="s06-pbt.html">Property-based testing</a>.
@@s011 Exercise 1: three LazyLists, two tests
@@s012 No code to write. The file already has two tests on <code>headOption</code> and, in the folder <code>subjects/</code>, three implementations of the LazyList. You change which one to import by commenting/uncommenting the lines at the top of the file, run the tests and see which one fails.
